    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d435">

                <pb facs="0594" n="488" sameAs="frus:frus1906p1/pg488"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Provisional Governor of
                        Cuba.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1906-10-06"><hi rendition="#italic">October 6,
                        1906</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inclose for your
                    information copy of a note from Mr. Quesada, the Cuban minister at this capital,
                    expressing his confidence in the right intentions of the American Government and
                    people in the matter of their intervention in Cuba, and stating that he will
                    remain at his post while he can serve Cuba and aid in promoting relations of
                    confidence and trust between the two Governments.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">E. Root.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
